{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: sequence aligment and prediction programs. Database analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (62.5%) to Aurein 2.3 V=G:25%; S=L: 13%. Mol Wt: 1660.979; GRAVY: 0.92; Mol Formula: C78H126N21O19; mol ex coeff: 5550. Activity: E. coli ATCC 25922 (MBC 17.5 uM), P. aeruginosa (MBC 35 uM), S. aureus ATCC 29213 (MBC 40 uM), E-faecalis ATCC 29212 (MBC >70 uM), B. cereus ATCC 6464 (MBC 70 uM). In vitro Toxicity: not hemo.lytic at 128 uM. Did not cause significant viability decrease for HaCat, MCF-7, and PC-3 after 24 h treatment up to 50 uM. Structure: helical in 30% TFE.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "36559073", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Pharmaceutics. 2022 Nov 23;14(12):2579. doi: 10.3390/pharmaceutics14122579. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03606", "source_id": "AP03606", "source_numeric_id": "03606", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03606", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Ramosin: The First Antibacterial Peptide Identified on Bolitoglossa ramosi Colombian Salamander.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
